  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDA20 Crisis Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Link to annual report: https://documents1.worldbank.org/curated/en/099050323190032975/pdf/BOSIB0a919239500a0be5404b8b274827b8.pdf</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale up support for the world&#x2019;s poorest countries to address worsening development challenges due to the overlapping global crises, particularly food insecurity and extreme climate events. The poorest and most vulnerable have been hit hardest by the global surge in energy and food prices and rising inflation exacerbated by Russia&#x2019;s invasion of Ukraine. The spillover of the invasion is further worsening the significant setbacks caused by COVID-19 and climate change, especially in Africa and the Middle East. The Crisis Facility will therefore provide financing to help countries respond to food insecurity, deal with economic shocks, address increasingly frequent and severe natural disasters, and respond to health emergencies and severe disease outbreaks.

20% will be allocated for SPUR (Special Program for Ukraine and Moldova Recovery) and 80% for CRW+ (Crisis Response Window Plus).</narrative>
  </description>
